# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editing sidecars and pre-edit snapshots (2026-07-14)
#
# These are development-tree working artifacts. They are never publishable and
# must not be promoted to C:\x64base. Observed leaking into staging as 815
# untracked files, dominated by dotref.hpp.bak_phase5_* and *.before_mdo_*.
#
# See docs/agents/CURRENT_TARGET.md and AI_PORTAL.md
# ("What C:\x64base Is - and Is Not").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.before_mdo_*
*.orig
*.rej
*.save
*.SAVE
*.save.txt

# Backup lanes - working copies, never publishable
/dottalkpp/data/backup/
**/backup/
# Dated pre-edit backups of tracked dirs (e.g. help.bak-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS/). The
# source dir is versioned; the timestamped snapshot is disposable scratch.
**/*.bak-[0-9]*/
**/*.bak-[0-9]*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LMDB index environments (2026-07-14)
#
# LMDB is a DERIVED index backend. It is materialized from the CDX container
# via SETLMDB (see src/cli/cmd_setlmdb.cpp: DbArea -> IndexManager ->
# CdxBackend -> LMDB env, stored as <stem>.cdx.d/).
#
# Measured 53 GB in dottalkpp/data/lmdb on 2026-07-14. It must never reach
# C:\x64base or GitHub. Publish the CDX; regenerate the LMDB locally with
# dottalkpp/data/scripts/mcc/mcc_build_x64_lmdb.dts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/dottalkpp/data/lmdb/
**/*.cdx.d/
# .mdb (LMDB env files) anywhere, not just under data/lmdb/. All OTHER valid
# dottalkpp file types (.dbf/.cdx/.dtx/.fpt/.dbt/.meta/...) are let THROUGH -- they
# may be tracked as fixtures/source tables. Only .mdb is excluded, because it is
# regenerable from the CDX container (SETLMDB) and can be huge. Matches the
# prepush-gate hard block on .mdb (member.derald ruling 2026-08-05).
**/*.mdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Probe and scratch index/table artifacts (2026-07-14)
#
# Generated by ad-hoc probe scripts. Never part of the runtime scaffold or the
# MCC sample set. These leaked into the first PR via directory-level git add.
# The runtime ships its directory STRUCTURE and the MCC/OG data -- not scratch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
zz_*
**/table.cnx
**/table.cdx
**/table.cdx.meta
*mixed.workspace*
# non-MCC test tables that live inside the sample dirs
/dottalkpp/data/dbf/x64/TEST64.dbf
/dottalkpp/data/dbf/TEST32.dbf
/dottalkpp/data/dbf/TESTVFP.dbf
/dottalkpp/data/dbf/BIGCHAR_TEST.dbf
/dottalkpp/data/dbf/X64SAMPLE.dbf

# Compiled runtime -- the repo ships the scaffold to BUILD the exe, not the exe
/dottalkpp/bin/dottalkpp.exe
**/*.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCC extracted originals (2026-07-14)
#
# data/dbf/og is DERIVED. extract_mcc_og.ps1 unpacks it from the canonical
# MyCommunityCollege.zip, which IS published. Publishing both would ship the
# same 84 KB twice and invite them to drift apart.
#
# The zip is the origin. og is a working copy of it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/dottalkpp/data/dbf/og/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch / tool working dirs at repo root (2026-07-25)
# These are agent/tool scratch, not project content. The data-subdir variants
# (/dottalkpp/data/tmp, /dottalkpp/data/.relations) were already ignored; the
# repo-root ones were not, which is why ~1,785 files showed untracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
/_tmp/
/.relations/
/.codex-tools/
/.codex-work/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch inside src/ and include/ (2026-07-25)
#
# Notes, chat dumps, session archives, and data files living in the SOURCE
# tree. These got swept into a commit by a directory-level git add (the
# AIF-050 backfill incident, force-push-repaired same day). Ignore the clear
# scratch categories so it cannot happen again.
#
# NOT ignored (left visible as untracked, promote or delete deliberately):
#   src/tests/*.cpp, src/reference/, src/schemas/, src/cli/cmd_transaction.cpp
#   and other plausible future source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORRECTED 2026-07-25, same day, by the rule in AIF-062. The first draft of this
# section ignored /src/AIPortal/, /src/**/*.patch and /src/**/*.dts as "scratch". That
# was the identical mistake the *.log rule made: src/AIPortal/sessions/ is the
# OUTSIDE-AI CHANGE PACKAGE INTAKE AREA, and the contract
# (labtalk/ai_portal/EXTERNAL_AI_CHANGE_PACKAGE_V1.md) requires the received archive be
# PRESERVED AS INTAKE EVIDENCE. 46 files were hidden, including AI_CHANGE_PACKAGE_*.md,
# BUILD_TEST_PLAN_*, closeouts, and 7 .patch deliverables. `.patch` and `.dts` are
# DELIVERABLE TYPES here, not noise -- never blanket-ignore them.
#
# What remains ignored is only what is genuinely disposable: loose prose dropped in the
# source tree, pre-edit sidecars, and binary/data blobs.

# prose/notes dropped into the source tree (CMakeLists.txt is unaffected:
# gitignore never hides tracked files, and new cmake files are *.txt-negated)
/src/**/*.txt
!/src/**/CMakeLists.txt
!/src/AIPortal/**
# src/url is a deliberate curated-URL home, not disposable prose -- track its .txt
!/src/url/**
/include/*.txt
# pre-edit sidecars only -- NOT .patch or .dts, which are deliverables
/src/**/*.before_image_web_defaults
# archives and binary data inside src/ and include/
/src/*.zip
/src/data/
/include/manuals/
# collection stubs parked under src/ (prose only; AIPortal is intake evidence, kept)
/src/psych/
/src/labtalk/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Untracked-triage v1 (2026-07-26): quiet regenerable/generated EXHAUST only.
# Verified zero collision with tracked files at add time (~2,284 untracked hidden).
# Deliberately does NOT ignore dottalkpp/data DBF/index TABLES: dbf/ help/ indexes/
# carry 84 tracked fixtures (a track-the-source-tables policy), and indexes/ is mixed
# (36 tracked / 144 cache) -- left for a later per-subtype decision. Also does NOT
# ignore *.patch / *.dts (AIPortal deliverables, per the AIF-062 note above).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# archive/backup trees (copies, never a source of truth)
docs/**/backups/
docs/**/_backups/
dottalkpp/docs/_backups/
# manual-generation run logs + generated per-step status files
docs/manuals/developer/manualgen/logs/
docs/manuals/developer/manualgen/MDO-*_STATUS.md
docs/manuals/developer/manualgen/PIP-*_STATUS.md
# regenerable RAM cache + legacy mcc DBF copies parked at repo root
dottalkpp/data/ram/
mcc/*.DBF
# stray root-level accidental python saves (e.g. "import sys.py")
/import*.py

# --- Untracked-triage v2 (2026-07-26): generated CSV + CDX metadata cache ---
# Generated report/candidate CSVs. 3 deliberately-tracked report CSVs
# (manualgen/reports/mdo_226_*, labtalk/reports/.../crosswalk_v1) stay tracked.
**/generated/**/*.csv
**/reports/**/*.csv
docs/manuals/developer/manualgen/**/*.csv
docs/maintenance/lanes/**/runs/**/*.csv
docs/**/candidates/**/*.csv
# Regenerable GPTbase bundle output (derive it, do not save it). The manifest and
# the generator are tracked; the produced bundle is not. See GPTBASE_BUNDLE_MANIFEST_V1.md.
docs/ai-friendly/gptbase_bundle_v1/
# Regenerable CDX metadata sidecars (0 tracked). The .cdx/.cnx binaries under
# indexes/ are left VISIBLE on purpose: mixed 36 tracked / 75 untracked -- a
# per-file call for a later pass.
dottalkpp/data/indexes/**/*.cdx.meta

# --- Registry fragment migration backups (2026-08-02) ---
# registry_fragments.py `migrate` copies the flat registries here before splitting, and
# leaves them behind on a failed verify so the state can be inspected. Timestamped, one
# per run, purely local safety copies -- never part of the history. Delete when satisfied.
labtalk/registries/_pre_fragment_backup_*/

# AIF-093: `.text` is the curated "chosen to travel" marker -- never ignore it.
# No rule above matches `.text`; this is an explicit durability guard (R1).
!**/*.text
